From 6440d84a68d20836d31f0e9dcbe380fd9d4604e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 11:47:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 53/53] win32u, winewayland: Avoid blocking managed dma-buf
 producers.

Track whether the Wayland consumer can accept frames and withhold managed frames while it is unknown or suspended. Share that state across overlapping swapchains and request it again after channel changes.

Keep managed image acquisition nonblocking so synchronous window changes cannot deadlock against the producer thread. Recreate only after a consumer-owned full ring remains stalled for the watchdog interval.

Adapted to the selective Wine-Wineland child-rendering series.

Original commit: 129fa64fc4491756b898463f1f3b7686e14a4a55
